<h3 id="icon-naming-conventions" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>Icon naming conventions</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#icon-naming-conventions" aria-label="Link to Icon naming conventions"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>TechCards</strong>: Use kebab-case (for example, <code>node-js</code>, <code>next-js</code>)</li>
<li><strong>DetailIconCards</strong>: Use camelCase or kebab-case as defined in the mapping</li>
<li><strong>File Requirements</strong>: Ensure SVG files exist in the correct directories</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="best-practices" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>Best practices</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#best-practices" aria-label="Link to Best practices"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Test your icons</strong>: Always verify that your chosen icon works in the target component</li>
<li><strong>Check both systems</strong>: If an icon doesn&#x27;t work in one system, try the other</li>
<li><strong>Use descriptive names</strong>: Choose icon names that clearly represent the technology or feature</li>
<li><strong>Document your choices</strong>: Keep track of which icons work in which components</li>
<li><strong>Fallback gracefully</strong>: Provide alternative text or descriptions when icons aren&#x27;t available</li>
</ol>
